   "args": {
    "text": "Verdict: supported\n\nThe cited Olah et al. (2020) work, *Zoom In: An Introduction to Circuits*, supports the description of studying weights and activations to understand how a model functions:\n\n- It studies neurons and directions in the space of neuron activations as potentially understandable features (distill:zoom-in/r1/b22). It examines which inputs make curve-detector neurons fire strongly or moderately (distill:zoom-in/r1/b36).\n- It studies circuits comprising linked features and the weights between them, explaining that understanding the connected features makes it possible to read algorithms from the weights (distill:zoom-in/r1/b69; distill:zoom-in/r1/b70).\n\nThe scope is exploratory: the authors acknowledge that they have only scratched the surface of understanding a single vision model (distill:zoom-in/r1/b11). Thus it supports the sentence’s description of the method, without establishing comprehensive understanding of models.\n\nI could not locate the separately cited Nanda et al. (2023) work in the library, so this verdict concerns Olah et al. only."
   },
