   "delta": "Verdict: supported\n\nThe cited Olah et al. (2020) work, *Zoom In: An Introduction to Circuits*, supports the description of studying weights and activations to understand a model:\n\n- **Activations:** It studies neurons and directions in the space of neuron activations as understandable features, and examines which inputs make curve-detector neurons fire strongly or moderately. distill:zoom-in/r1/b22; distill:zoom-in/r1/b36.\n- **Weights:** It studies circuits comprising linked features and their connecting weights, explaining that understanding those features allows researchers to read algorithms from the weights. distill:zoom-in/r1/b69; distill:zoom-in/r1/b70.\n\nThis supports the sentence’s description of the method. Its demonstrated scope is limited: the authors acknowledge that they have only scratched the surface of understanding a single vision model. distill:zoom-in/r1/b11.\n\nI could not locate the separately cited Nanda et al. (2023) work in the library, so this verdict concerns Olah et al. only."
